L wrote:
> Here's _my_ way to make NetHack harder:
>
> * Two words: stronger monsters. Currently the only creatures capable of
> busting a character at midgame time are jabberwocks and minotaurs. Tut,
> tut. If the "Hell-only" monsters' attacks contained several d10's or
> d20's, we'd solve half of the problem right there.

The problem here is that simple damage just isn't a deterrent to people
who want to power up forever.  Altar camp until you have a bazillion
HP.  And it penalizes speed runs and other interesting approaches
disproportionately.  I'd be more in favor of limiting how much the
player can buff up--a max HP cap, or diminishing returns so that the
probability of getting more max HP from altars/potions/etc goes down
the higher your HP are.

That said, a few more rare hard-hitting monsters that a skilled player
could avoid or deal with from afar make sense as a deterrent to someone
blindly doing Valk Smash!  Make some monsters that are immune to
physical weapons, so there's a reason to actually use up attack wands
in combat (and to save some in the mid-game).

Eliminate Elbereth in Gehennom--the lady can't help you here.

Also, if you make Gehennom much shorter then making some rather tough
monsters is more appealing.

> * Make it so that intrinsic resistances are less powerful than
> extrinsic resistances. Like, they only halve the damage instead of
> negating it entirely. I actually have a patch that does this, but I
> haven't released it yet.

I like this idea for fire/cold/lightning.  Not sure about, say,
sleep/poison.

> * Remove the ability to unrestrict weapon skills. It severely breaks
> roleplaying and character differentiation. Also, your god should only
> give you a weapon artifact if you can already reach "skilled" in its
> weapon skill.

Yes.  Also forbid wishing for Quest artifacts.

Other ideas:

Make unique monsters tougher.  Demogorgon and Rodney are threats, as
are the riders.  Everything else is pretty laughable.  Especially make
Vlad a threat, but also Juiblex (digging only gets you out of him and
damages him some, but not to 1HP), Orcus (maybe his /Death is an
artifact wand that has a chance against reflection/MR), etc.  Perhaps
make =FreeAction less potent vs. paralyzation, at least paralyzation
from uniques and the high priest of Moloch--still work against other
priests, gel cubes, etc.

Up the HP, lower the AC, and make them have some combat/spell threat to
a kitted-out player.  Also, make most of them _not_ do the "teleport to
the stairs" bit; that's interesting at first, but when everything is
doing it then you know how to deal with it and you're just doing the
same (boring) motions repeatedly.

Eliminate some instadeath options; since there are only a handful of
dangerous monsters, players easily stockpile enough instadeaths to take
them down as soon as their seen and avoid the danger entirely.  Make
more of the uniques have higher resistance to wand/finger of death, and
stoning.  And have them tough enough the !paralysis is helpful but not
an "almost instadeath".

Make only 1-2 maze levels, and have them undiggable and no-teleport.
Make Gehennom a couple mazes, Juiblex swamp, Asmodeus, Orcus, the
towers, and VS level.  Throw a bigroom in there, but with
Gehennom-level monsters--maybe add a couple of choke points so that
running through it is hard without facing the monsters, but no
corriders where you can avoid being surrounded.  Make it a short mad
dash, with some real threats on each level (demon lords souped up, a
"Minotaur King" in the labyrinths, tougher Vlad, Rodney).  And maybe
increase the number of random items on those levels to compensate for
fewer monster drops.

Shorter Gehennom makes the mysterious force less annoying as well,
which is easier but mainly avoids tedium.  Maybe make the ghosts of the
demon lords (or something) appear on the way up.

(I'd also make the amulet no-teleport-control, but still allow
teleport.  That way you could level-teleport to avoid some of the
trudge to the top, but you can't just jump to level one without burning
a ton of teleports trying to get there randomly).



